{"artifact_reads":[{"digest_matched":true,"path":".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/ossie-relational-bundle-plan.md"},{"digest_matched":true,"path":".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/close-results.md"},{"digest_matched":true,"path":".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/close-delta.md"}],"concern_count":12,"disposition":"revise","reviewer_id":"qwen","schema_version":2,"summary":"The three artifacts are coherent about what shipped and state the missing external acceptance plainly ('External acceptance is missing. ... No reporter run is cited. D10 has not been sent.'), so no concern is blocking. Twelve concerns remain, all against evidence sufficiency and internal consistency: the close reports the project guard block red (exit 1) and calls it pre-existing without citing a baseline, while the plan makes declaration of new modules in tools/gnd_layers.json and dev/components/ a deliverable; plan §11 A8 says the no-table path writes 'the ontology's three files and a note' while the delta and results say only three files, leaving the note's home, publish-group, collision and size-bound status unstated; the delivered scale test's actual size is unrecorded and A6's '5x' matches neither rule 2's reporter's scale nor OB2-C4's '1,400 tables and 4,500 fact types'; the lane labelled '(the plan §9 rows of all five phases)' omits the RF7 input-policy tests A3 added, the PINNED.json digest test §9 names and the disclosure tests §5 requires, and the guard block's 16 files are unnamed; the no-review-opinion inventory omits src/gnd/export/ossie_relational.py even though A14's quoting fix and OB5-Q2 put it in this review's scope; predicate 6's 'No second home states a rule' and predicate 3's one-home clause cite only doc tests, a build and a link check, which would not fail if a rule were duplicated; and D5's ruling, the oracle lane's commit provenance, OB5-Q1's disposition, A14's pointer to §2.2, A16's ratio arithmetic and the