{"concern_id":"close-guard-block-red-asserted-not-evidenced","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/close-results.md","location":"'Exit gates on `main` at `f5462783`' table, guard-block row","observation":"The row reads: \"the project guard block (16 files) | `1 failed, 865 passed, 2 deselected in 124.04s`, exit 1. The failure is `tests/test_development_scaffold.py::test_reference_closure_and_declared_bootstrap`, the known red, which fails on main before this milestone.\" No baseline commit, run digest, issue id or quoted output supports 'fails on main before this milestone', and the 16 files are not named."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-relational-bundle/notes/ossie-relational-bundle-plan.md","location":"§3 'Dependencies and artifact homes', Rmap row; §8 step 3","observation":"The plan makes declaration a deliverable -- \"Rmap | new `src/gnd/rmap.py`, assigned in `tools/gnd_layers.json` and `dev/components/`\" -- and §8 requires \"focused tests, plus the issue-171 guard list\". A test named `test_reference_closure_and_declared_bootstrap` is precisely the check that would fail if a module or schema added by this milestone (rmap.py, ossie_relational.py, physical_binding.py, mapping.json, physical-binding.schema.json) were not declared, so the pre-existing claim is load-bearing."}],"recommendation":"Before the close record is written, either cite the baseline evidence for the known red (the pre-milestone commit where the same test id fails, or the tracked owner issue for it) or repair the reference-closure/bootstrap declaration for the files this milestone added and re-run the guard block to green; also name the 16 guard-block files so the exit-1 result can be attributed.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"high","title":"Guard block exits 1 at the close and its 'known red, pre-existing' status is asserted without evidence"}
